 The pages under `docs/` are this repository's source of truth for people and coding agents. This page says which page
 owns each fact; read it before writing one.
+
+## Kinds
+
+Each fact has one owning page; other pages link to it. Every page opens with who reads it, when, what it says and
+why it exists. Directory guides list their pages.
+
+| Kind | Owns | Type and required content |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| [Decisions](adrs/README.md) (`adrs/`) | Why a foundation was chosen. A record qualifies when reversing the decision changes more than one feature or module; a replaceable library choice alone does not qualify. | Explanation: Context (what happened and the forces), Options (each option and why it lost or won), Decision (choice and reason, including the implementing product), Consequences (benefits, costs and constraints). Files are `NNNN-<slug>.md`. |
+| [Features](features/README.md) (`features/`) | What one unit of behavior does, including rules and limits. Reasons below the decision-record bar live here. | Reference: sections follow the behavior; Shaped by links the decisions behind it. |
+| [Runbooks](runbooks/README.md) (`runbooks/`) | What an operator does for one trigger. | How-to: Before you begin, Steps with expected output for each, If it fails; name the owner. |
+| [Architecture](architecture.md) | The parts and connections no single source file shows. | Explanation: Parts and How they connect; link decisions for the reasons behind structural choices. |
+
+[Glossary](glossary.md) owns shared terms and rejected synonyms. Code and contracts own implementation details;
+documentation links to them. Issue discussions supply history, but the owning documentation page preserves the
+reasoning a maintainer needs.
